// The projection of a roster.
//
// This is a vocabulary of CLAIMS, not of row shapes: a claim needs a speaker,
// and there are two.
//
//   Anonymous     — the server applied the anonymous projection. The caller's
//                   session was absent, expired or revoked
//                   (services/server/src/api/handlers/vpn.rs:40-70).
//   Full          — the server applied the full projection; the nine extra
//                   fields were dropped by the type, not withheld by the
//                   server (RFC-047 §2.4).
//   LocalFallback — NO SERVER WAS ASKED. The client narrowed these rows
//                   itself, from a fallback channel that carries no server
//                   statement. This is NOT the same claim as `Anonymous` and
//                   the two must never be conflated: one is "your session is
//                   not in force", the other is "the control plane is
//                   unreachable".
//
// The Rust type is `shadowmesh_core::NodeProjection`, whose variants are
// `Anonymous`, `Full` and `LocalFallback` — the names here MUST match them,
// because the generated scaffolding derives this enum's FFI converter from the
// Rust type's variants, IN THIS ORDER. A mismatch does not fail the build; it
// silently mis-maps the discriminants, which is the worst failure mode there
// is (RFC-049 §15.6.4).
enum NodeProjection {
  "Anonymous",
  "Full",
  "LocalFallback",
};

// ── F102 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The roster envelope. The projection is the server's own statement about
// which projection it applied, and it is carried in the body because a body is
// what a client parses (RFC-047 §2.2).
//
// The accessor returns the ENVELOPE, not the rows. A separate projection
// accessor would be two requests and two answers that could disagree; an
// out-parameter is not expressible in UDL; a projection *parameter* would be a
// request for a projection the server does not grant on request (RFC-043 R2).
//
// FROZEN 2026-10-21 by RFC-049 §15. Changing either of the two signatures
// below requires a new RFC: the Android client's roster path depends on them.
dictionary NodeRoster {
  NodeProjection projection;
  sequence<PublicNode> nodes;
};

// FROZEN 2026-10-21 by RFC-050 §8.1. Changing `GlobalManifest`'s row type,
// or `PublicNode`'s four fields, requires a new RFC.
//
// ⚠️ The row type is `PublicNode`, and it was `VPNNode`. RFC-050 §2.2: the
// manifest is a **listing** surface, and a listing carries `PublicNode` —
// the same row type the roster route uses. `VPNNode` is the **connect**
// surface's row, and it carries eight mandatory fields; the anonymous
// projection's row carries four, so an anonymous manifest body **did not
// deserialize at all** and the `"projection"` the server sent correctly was
// never read.
//
// ⇒ The connect material comes from the authenticated
// `GET /api/v1/config/:server_id` (RFC-043 R2, applied by RFC-050 §2.4).
// It is NOT optionalised, NOT synthesised, and NOT defaulted here.
dictionary GlobalManifest {
  NodeProjection projection;
  sequence<PublicNode> nodes;
  sequence<AnycastVip> anycast_vips;
  string version;
};

